From 0ca95838b15b9d7029457fa8e5fefc13e8d2c9d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Bozik <robertbozik@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:50:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] libcamera: software_isp: Add a linear toe to the gamma
 curve

A plain power function has an infinite slope at zero, so the darkest
tones get the largest amplification: the noise and the positive bias
left by clipping the noise at the black level end up as a grey-green
veil over the shadows of a dark scene.

Let the tuning file add a linear segment near black with gammaOffset,
in the style of the sRGB transfer function: the curve becomes
(1 + offset) * x ^ (1 / gamma) - offset above the point where its slope
matches the line through the origin, and that line below it. The IPA
computes the threshold and the slope, both debayers apply them. The
default offset of 0 keeps the plain power function.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5 [Claude Code]
